    "turn_text": "we say, do not put your head up, we will lob it off. They're almost conditioning this bullying into, ooh, we gotta be more quiet. So there's a lot of hope in the future, but the future actually lies with the young people today. It lies with your generation. And probably the generation just behind you. Because it took us many years to get here. It's going to take us many years to get out of it. But having a voice and standing up and feeling as if, hey, you don't have to wait, you don't have to just go to work nine to five, keep your head down, you can get involved. I know you have gotten involved, but being a ambassador collectively together, getting together, having those conversations and then joining organizations that bring down the median age of of the groups that are out there that are fighting for freedom, that are fighting for the Constitution. If that happens, the future will be very, very bright. But I think that it's going to take your generation and young people under the age of 30, being a better example than the geriatric dimwet we have in the Oval Office right now.",
