    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46917.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 164,
    "turn_text": "Well, they're not in the polls. And this is the problem that I have with the polls is that the polls aren't representative of what's really happening in our country and we're happening in our society. Usually take a group of the same people. They ask the same questions too. They can manipulate those polls to actually push the direction or sentiment that they want the public to feel one way or another. But I'm actually closer to it. So I get to see my daughter and see young people. I sat in a, I took a bunch of kids between the ages 16 and 18. I took them to the gun store or the gun range and we shot an automatic weapon, right? So there was probably, I think, I want to say there was probably 12 to 15 of them there. Yeah, and 14 guys there and kids there and one of them said why I'm more liberal and he still shot the machine gun had a good time and then the other 13 of those kids that went to the gun store some of them were uncomfortable with it but had a dinner with them got to spend a little time with them and talk to them about why these rights are so important and every one of those kids walked away with this feeling that, hey, I didn't even know that was a thing. I didn't know the Second Amendment was that people fought and died for it. These are kids that are going to high school. So I think it's our job, the older generation, it's our job to be a better example and to spout truth. It's also our job to make sure that there's a fundamental value of faith. in what we do. It's our fault when kids don't have a foundation of God. It's our fault. We allow our society to go that direction, we allow our schools to go that direction, and we push kids to basically wonder what is life all about, which is why you have higher suicide rates, you have higher drug use rates. I think that they're just searching for a compass to point them in true North. And so I think that, Mike, your generation is an exciting generation because There's so much that can happen if you knew it could happen. There's so many people that actually stand on the left-hand side of the aisle because I think it's the most popular, not because I think it's right, but because I just think it's popular, not recognizing that courage is more infectious and fear. And if they speak up and move towards that, then other people will follow.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "The current polling data does not reflect the actual state of affairs in the country and society.",
